{"name":"Sweet Flag","hex":"#674196","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sweet flag","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A perennial wetland plant, Acorus calamus, with an aromatic medicinal root, formerly used to strew floors."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweet_flag"}],"entries":[{"title":"Acorus calamus","blocks":[{"text":"Acorus calamus is a species of flowering plant. It is a tall wetland monocot of the family Acoraceae, in the genus Acorus. Although used in traditional medicine over centuries to treat digestive disorders and pain, it has no clinical evidence of safety or efficacy and may be toxic if ingested, and so has been commercially banned for use in food in the United States."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Acorus_calamus1.jpg/330px-Acorus_calamus1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acorus_calamus"},{"title":"Flag","blocks":[{"text":"A flag is a piece of fabric with distinctive colours and design, often flown from a pole and used for symbolic, signalling, or decorative purposes. The term flag is also used to refer to the graphic design employed on such pieces of fabric. The study of flags is known as \"vexillology\" from the Latin vexillum, meaning \"flag\" or \"banner\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/United_Nations_Flags_-_cropped.jpg/330px-United_Nations_Flags_-_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flag"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Acorus_calamus1.jpg/500px-Acorus_calamus1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Acorus_calamus1.jpg/500px-Acorus_calamus1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbna